  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Morocco Earthquake Emergency Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On Friday, September 8th, a powerful 6.8 magnitude earthquake struck Morocco, killing at least 2,800 people and leaving another 2,500 people injured. IsraAID arrived in Morocco less than 48 hours after the earthquake to begin initial assessments, meet with community partners, and distribute essential humanitarian aid. IsraAID is further assessing urgent needs in Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene, and Mental Health and Psychosocial Support.</narrative>
  </description>
